+# Original-order priority-key caching: isolated causal intervention
+
+Goal remains full-update joint ready-task / replica / gradient-lifetime planning. Previous goal turn made progress: completed ABI2 correctness and a matched negative screening pair; it did not achieve the full goal.
+
+This child starts at raw-control@693f7fc. Branch research/step-lifetime-priority-cache; old source/compiled variants/evidence remain read-only. One production-kernel change only: evaluate each immutable placement-derived GradientKey once, then retain the original stable insertion sort. No routing/quota/task order/owner/transport/FP32 accumulation or resource changes. Same private ABI2; no ready polling value is cached.
+
+Reference worker ep8-cap64-lifetime-raw-control-v2 SHA72653abf3c22fb951624dd5dc420c488d2511d1c22e5e605a3621cb4210502bf is copied into a new isolated remote lane. Candidate gets a NEW variant ep8-cap64-lifetime-priority-cache-v1. Common source/host/framework and build options are held constant; build manifests explicitly distinguish compiled reference and candidate header hashes. Per-process source-tree identity is not presented as the baseline binary's build-source identity.
+
+First preserve the order oracle on actual plans, build, run independent output/dx/dp/dW gates including empty owners/remote-only contributions, then three complete-model updates with FP32 gradients. Only then run a narrow matched TimerOFF pilot on L4 EP8 E256 K8 H4096 F1024 S16384/rank GA4/W2 recv262144, common90GiB limit. Per process25updates,5warmup20measured,8rank-max wall time. Qualify then compare the cached public path; follow with native anchor/fixed-home controls if evidence warrants. No 108matrix or new-policy claims from a common kernel optimization.
+
+If the candidate changes numerical semantics or does not improve complete updates, retain failure/negative evidence and proceed to the already-proposed service-admission/group-delivery causal controls. Any useful common optimization is opened to all applicable baselines before claiming a joint planner win.
+
+Remote isolation: new task directory/container/SO paths, shared device-jobs lock and actual occupancy checks; no other task termination or library replacement. All artifacts stay in this project, summaries only in codexwork. No future routes or optimizer-owner changes.
